# Beispiele – mit "HTTP-Client: Create Environment File" eine Umgebung anlegen
@user = janos

### Einfacher GET
GET https://httpbin.org/get
    ?id={{$random.integer(1, 100)}}
    &trace={{$uuid}}
Accept: application/json

> {%
  client.test("Status 200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200, "Status " + response.status));
  client.log("id =", jsonPath(response.body, "$.args.id"));
%}

### POST mit JSON und globaler Variable
POST https://httpbin.org/post
Content-Type: application/json

{"user": "{{user}}", "ts": {{$timestamp}}}

> {%
  client.global.set("echoUser", response.body.json.user);
%}

### Pre-Request-Skript mit HMAC-Signatur
< {%
  const sig = crypto.hmac.sha256().withTextSecret("secret").updateWithText(request.url.tryGetSubstituted()).digest().toHex();
  request.variables.set("signature", sig);
%}
GET https://httpbin.org/headers
X-Signature: {{signature}}
X-User: {{echoUser}}
